(4) The locale defect is dead — reproduced the adversarial lane's scenario
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
PASS, by execution, not inspection.

(4a) Static: `grep -rn "toLocaleString" web/templates/components/whatif/`
returns exactly 5 call sites, every one locale-pinned:
  portfolio-settings.html:170   (base * multiplier).toLocaleString('en-US', {min/maxFractionDigits:2})
  quick-adjust-scripts.html:12  '$' + Math.round(v).toLocaleString('en-US')
  healthcare-person.html:81,121,148  '$' + Number(this.value).toLocaleString('en-US')
`grep -rn "toLocaleString()\|toLocaleString(undefined" web/templates/` returns
ZERO lines across the whole template tree (not just whatif), and the same grep
over web/static/js/ returns zero. rate-assumptions.html has zero toLocaleString
(it routes through `${formatWholeDollars(spending)}` at line 866).

(4b) Dynamic: a Node probe reads the template files off disk, extracts the
formatter source VERBATIM by regex (no hand-transcription) and evals it, run as
`LC_ALL=de_DE.UTF-8 LANG=de_DE.UTF-8 node locale_probe.js <tree>`:
  EXTRACTED_SOURCE: "function formatWholeDollars(v) {\n    return '$' + Math.round(v).toLocaleString('en-US');\n}"
  node default locale = de-DE
  formatWholeDollars(7386.5)  = $7,387      want $7,387      PASS
  formatWholeDollars(7386)    = $7,386      want $7,386      PASS
  formatWholeDollars(9232.5)  = $9,233      want $9,233      PASS
  formatWholeDollars(1234567) = $1,234,567  want $1,234,567  PASS
  CONTROL locale-less: $7.387          <-- the defect, reproduced
  healthcare inline handlers found: 3
    handler[0] on "7387" = $7,387  PASS
    handler[1] on "7387" = $7,387  PASS
    handler[2] on "7387" = $7,387  PASS
  portfolio phase-amount expr: "(base * multiplier).toLocaleString('en-US', {...})"
    portfolio phase amount(7386,1.25) = 9,232.50  PASS
  LOCALE_PROBE_PASS ; PROBE_EXIT=0

The CONTROL line is the decisive evidence: in the SAME process, under the SAME
de-DE default locale, the pre-fix locale-less call yields "$7.387" (dot
grouping, which would overwrite the server's "$7,386"/"$7,387" on first input
event) while every shipped call site yields comma grouping. Node honours
LC_ALL here — verified independently:
`LC_ALL=de_DE.UTF-8 node -e "..."` printed
  default locale: de-DE / bare: 7.387 / undef: 7.387
so the harness really was in a de-DE locale, and both the bare and the
`undefined`-locale forms are demonstrably broken there.

Caveat stated plainly: this is Node/ICU with the formatter extracted from the
templates, not a real browser. The brief authorised exactly this reproduction.

